  <prompt>
    Implement FR-07 apply-side. Before applying ANY AI-returned operation, validate EVERY returned
    paraId/offset against the LIVE document (the current editor/projection state, post-concurrent-edit).
    An operation whose anchor is unvalidatable — unknown paraId, out-of-range offset, or a range that no
    longer exists — MUST surface as a REVIEW COMMENT, never be silently placed. The last resort is fuzzy
    re-anchor via `Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs` bands (AUTO / REVIEW / ORPHAN with the
    ambiguity guard): a confident fuzzy match may re-anchor; an ambiguous or below-threshold match hits the
    ambiguity guard and surfaces as a comment rather than auto-placing. NO text-search placement anywhere
    (invariant I-7) — fuzzy content-match survives ONLY as the below-threshold surface-as-comment last resort.

    Reuse `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` (a KEEP asset) as the fuzzy layer — do NOT reimplement bands. This
    is envelope-only: engine FROZEN (ADR-039, no new dispatch endpoint), AI dispatch via
    `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only (ADR-013, no fork, no AI-internal injection). Client fetches via
    `@spaarke/auth` (ADR-028).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior full-stack engineer: React/TypeScript (the client AI apply path built in 040) + .NET 8
    (`AnnotationReanchorService` bands + ambiguity guard). Understands the R4 rule that a returned anchor is
    a claim to be VALIDATED against the live doc, and that an unvalidatable op is surfaced for human review —
    never text-searched into place, never silently dropped.
  </role>

  <goal>
    An AI apply path where every returned operation's paraId/offset is validated against the live document
    before apply: a valid anchor applies cleanly; an out-of-range/unknown anchor is REFUSED and surfaced as a
    review comment; a confident fuzzy match (via `AnnotationReanchorService` AUTO band) may re-anchor while an
    ambiguous match hits the ambiguity guard and surfaces rather than auto-placing. No text-search placement
    remains anywhere in the apply path.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 (AI paragraph): "on return, rebase the bookmark to its current position, validate every
      returned paraId/offset against the live doc, then apply. Unvalidatable ops surface as a review comment
      (fuzzy last resort), never silently placed." Invariant I-7: no text-search anchoring in the write path;
      fuzzy content-match survives ONLY as a below-threshold surface-as-comment last resort. This task
      consumes the resolved bookmark + returned operations from task 040 (the capture half) and adds the
      validation + fuzzy-fallback gate before apply. `AnnotationReanchorService` already implements the
      AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN bands + ambiguity guard + "never silently drop" — reuse it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx — the apply step: gate each returned operation through validation before applying; surface unvalidatable ops as review comments</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.ts — extend (from 040) with the validate-before-apply gate consuming the resolved bookmark + returned operations</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — KEEP asset: fuzzy re-anchor bands (AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN) + ambiguity guard + never-silently-drop; the last-resort fuzzy layer — REUSE, do not reimplement</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts — resolve/validate a returned paraId against the live editor state</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/ — task 040 resolved bookmark + returned JSON operations (the input to this gate)</file>
      <file role="dependency-output">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ — the AI facade seam (envelope-only; no new endpoint, no fork)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/design.md §5 (AI paragraph — validate then apply; fuzzy last resort)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/spec.md FR-07, NFR-02</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">Generate-window bookmark + resolve-on-return + returned JSON operations — the capture half this apply gate consumes.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-07">Before applying any AI-returned operation, MUST validate every returned paraId/offset against the LIVE document; unvalidatable ops (unknown paraId / out-of-range offset / vanished range) MUST surface as a review comment, NEVER be silently placed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / NFR-02 / project I-7">ZERO text-search in the write path. Fuzzy content-match via `AnnotationReanchorService` survives ONLY as the below-threshold surface-as-comment last resort; an ambiguous match MUST hit the ambiguity guard and surface, never auto-place.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / KEEP asset">REUSE `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` (AUTO/REVIEW/ORPHAN bands + ambiguity guard) as the fuzzy layer — MUST NOT reimplement or fork the band logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 / project">Engine FROZEN — no new AI dispatch endpoint, no AI catalog change; envelope-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">AI dispatch via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only — no fork of `Services/Ai/`; no `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing injection into `Services/Compose/` or the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / project">Client apply-path fetches use `@spaarke/auth`; no hand-rolled token handling.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021 / project">Any surfaced review-comment / apply UI is Fluent UI v9 and MUST render correctly in dark mode (theme tokens; no hard-coded colors).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Client component/unit tests exercise real editor state; if the BFF apply/validate path changes, add/update a seam slice in `tests/integration/seam/Compose/`. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
