    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Fuzzy re-anchor bands + ambiguity guard" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs">
        AUTO applies a confident match; REVIEW/ORPHAN surface; the ambiguity guard refuses to auto-place an ambiguous match and never silently drops — reuse as the last-resort fuzzy layer for unvalidatable AI anchors.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="paraId validation" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/paraIdExtension.ts">
        Resolve a returned paraId against the live editor state to decide validated / needs-fuzzy / surface-as-comment.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor (frontend + bff-api + docx; xhigh; sonnet). Load the knowledge files + design §5. Read `AnnotationReanchorService.cs` bands + ambiguity guard and the task 040 apply hook. State the Placement Justification (validation/apply is pure; AI dispatch stays behind PublicContracts).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Validate returned anchors">For each returned operation, validate its paraId + offset/range against the LIVE document. Classify: VALID (apply), or UNVALIDATABLE (unknown paraId / out-of-range / vanished range → fuzzy fallback).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Fuzzy fallback via reanchor bands">For unvalidatable ops, run the `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy layer: an AUTO-band confident match may re-anchor; a REVIEW/ORPHAN or ambiguity-guard hit surfaces as a review comment. NEVER auto-place an ambiguous match; NEVER text-search a placement.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Apply validated + surface the rest">Apply the validated (and AUTO-re-anchored) operations at their anchors; render the surfaced ops as review comments in the editor. Ensure NO path silently places an unvalidatable op (fire the escalation trigger if one is found).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Tests">Author component/unit tests (real editor state): valid anchor applies cleanly; out-of-range/unknown anchor is refused + surfaced; ambiguous fuzzy match hits the ambiguity guard and surfaces. If the BFF apply/validate path changed, add/update the `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` slice. Include an ADR-021 dark-mode check on any surfaced-comment UI.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Verify + index">`npm run build:prod` the shared lib (+ `dotnet build` if BFF touched); run tests + Tier-1 NetArchTest. Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any code path that would SILENTLY PLACE an unvalidatable operation (unknown paraId, out-of-range offset, or an ambiguous fuzzy match) instead of surfacing it for review — STOP and escalate per root §6. Silent placement violates FR-07 / NFR-02 / I-7 and is a §6 escalation, not a judgment call to make locally.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiGenerateBookmark.ts (validate-before-apply gate + fuzzy fallback wiring)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeAiToolbar.tsx (apply gated by validation; surfaced review comments)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/hooks/useAiApplyValidation.test.ts</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/ (seam slice if the BFF apply/validate path changed)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Every AI-returned operation's paraId/offset is validated against the LIVE document before apply; a valid anchor applies cleanly at its intended location.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An out-of-range or unknown anchor is REFUSED and surfaced as a review comment (via the `AnnotationReanchorService` REVIEW/ORPHAN path) — it is NOT mis-placed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an ambiguous fuzzy match hits the `AnnotationReanchorService` ambiguity guard and surfaces as a comment rather than auto-placing; no unvalidatable op is ever silently placed or silently dropped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Zero text-search placement remains in the apply path (NFR-02 / I-7); fuzzy content-match is used only as the below-threshold surface-as-comment last resort; `AnnotationReanchorService` is reused (not reimplemented).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AI dispatch routes through `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` only — no new endpoint, no AI catalog change (ADR-039), no fork / AI-internal injection (ADR-013); Tier-1 NetArchTest green if BFF touched.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Surfaced review-comment UI renders correctly in Fluent v9 dark mode (ADR-021); client tests + any `tests/integration/seam/Compose/` slice pass; builds green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Valid anchor applies cleanly">
      <steps>AI returns an operation whose paraId/offset resolves in the live doc; apply it.</steps>
      <expected>The operation lands at the intended paraId+offset; no comment is surfaced.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Out-of-range anchor is refused + surfaced">
      <steps>AI returns an operation referencing an unknown paraId (or an out-of-range offset).</steps>
      <expected>The operation is NOT applied; it surfaces as a review comment (REVIEW/ORPHAN band); the document text is unchanged at that location.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Ambiguous fuzzy match hits the ambiguity guard">
      <steps>AI returns an operation whose anchor only fuzzy-matches ambiguously (multiple candidate spans).</steps>
      <expected>The ambiguity guard refuses to auto-place; the op surfaces as a review comment rather than landing on a guessed span.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Render the surfaced review-comment affordance under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>The comment/review UI uses theme tokens and is legible in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Apply half of FR-07; the capture half (bookmark + resolve-on-return) is task 040. Success Criterion 3
    (AI drift-proof; bad anchors refused) is proven by task 042's automated ProseMirror test. Run
    `/conflict-check` before any BFF-touching PR.
  </notes>

